 ## Overview
-Isogeometric Volume Rendering is a method for the interactive visualization of isogeometric analysis (IGA) results, ensuring correct, pixel-accurate geometry of the volume including its bounding surfaces [S1]. It extends classic volume rendering to isogeometric volumes where both geometry and scalar field are given in terms of splines (NURBS, B-splines) [S1]. Unlike voxelized methods which suffer from block-like structures and high memory demands, this method provides pixel-accurate outer surfaces and avoids the loss of geometrically exact representation [S1].
+Isogeometric Volume Rendering is a method for the interactive visualization of isogeometric analysis (IGA) results, ensuring correct, pixel-accurate geometry of the volume including its bounding surfaces [S1]. It extends classic volume rendering to isogeometric volumes where both geometry and scalar field are given in terms of splines (NURBS, B-splines) [S1]. Unlike voxelized methods which suffer from block-like structures and high memory demands, this method provides pixel-accurate outer surfaces and avoids the loss of geometrically exact representation [S1]. It builds on [Pre-filtered Cubic B-spline Interpolation](13450-pre-filtered-cubic-b-spline-interpolation.md) [S1].
 
